2026-08-24T20:57:11Z	tried	what=the bridge credential bootstraps itself	config=tmhaul credential check|serve|selftest; serve runs on the devserver under cron (@reboot plus every 15 minutes, one instance by lock dir), reads the box registry from the repo, and pushes to any live box that lacks the file	produced=deleted the credential from the running box twice: the first time the devserver's --once pass installed it (mode 600, 160 bytes, owner vjeux); the second time nobody intervened at all and the 5-minute cycle healed it within one period. In between, the status page said DEGRADED and banking_degraded fired	claim=MEASURED	control=tmhaul credential selftest is the arm that matters: a delivery to an unreachable host must REFUSE, its reason must be a category rather than a transport body, and an absent file must read Absent rather than ok. Plus the positive control of this box's own working credential, so the three refusals are not passing vacuously on a box where everything fails	why=An otherwise autonomous rotation with one manual file copy is not autonomous, and the goal is months unattended. The interesting part is the direction: an OD cannot reach a devserver, so this could not be a pull by the box that needs the file — the machine that HAS the credential pushes it, aimed by a registry the repo already publishes. Hostnames are not secrets; the credential never touches the repo, a log, a paste or an error body.	node=42504
